meta {
  name: Create a review
  type: http
  seq: 57
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/reviews
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  seed: 1
  ~locale: 
  ~conflict: 
  ~delay: 
  ~trickle: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
  ~auth: 
}

body:json {
  {
    "productId": 4171,
    "userId": 7204,
    "rating": 1,
    "title": "95bl",
    "body": "xpGcS"
  }
}

docs {
  Validates the body and answers with the new review: the next id after the dataset's last, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and a `Location` header. Fields the server sets are ignored if sent.

  `productId` must name a record in `/products`, and `userId` must name a record in `/users` at the same `seed` and `locale`, or the write answers `422`.

  By default nothing is stored, so a later read returns the same data as before and the response is what the write would have produced. With the session on (`--session`, `REST_IN_PIECES_SESSION=true` or `createApp({ session: true })`), the change is kept in memory and later reads at the same `seed` and `locale` see it, until `POST /reset`. A session that is full answers `507`.
}
